{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Let them make no more work for the sacred contribution.</b> He did not proclaim that they should not bring freewill offerings as they wished, but he proclaimed that they should do no more work — such as the work of spinning, of which it says וַיָּבִיאוּ מַטְוֶה (Exodus 35:25), or the work of preparing the wood, of which it says עֲצֵי שִׁטִּים לְכָל מְלֶאכֶת הָעֲבֹדָה הֵבִיאוּ (Exodus 35:24), or the preparation of the skins and the like."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:17.830351773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}